us Merchandise Store Student Services and Amenities Fee Bond Sports Centre Group exercise classes Personal training Sports Centre memberships Student housing options Student rights and responsibilities Complaints involving the behaviour of others Advocacy and support Appeals Your responsibilities Your rights Student conduct and misconduct Student surveys Graduate Outcomes Survey Student Experience Survey Opportunities Outbound student mobility Partnering with DFAT Exchange at Bond Participating institutions Asia Europe North America Information sessions Exchange blog How to apply Financial information and funding New Colombo Plan Scholarship 2027 Preparing to go Overseas Back at Bond Frequently asked questions Mooting at Bond What is mooting Mooting opportunities Mooting accolades Grants and scholarships Elite Athlete Fund Student Hardship Grant Student Opportunity Fund Frequently asked questions FinTech Hub training Bond Legal Clinics Program The Bond Law Clinic Climate Sustainability Clinic Criminal Law Clinic How to apply Internet Law Research Clinic My Community Legal Clinic Beyond Bond Graduation Preparing to graduate Conferral dates Ceremony information Ceremony videos Graduation booklets Graduation documents MyBond Library iLearn Staff iLearn Library Email Staff Intranet Online Service Catalogue Careers at Bond People Connect Alumni About Bond alumni Online Bond community The Arch Industry and partners Global education partners Sponsorship opportunities News and events News Events Contact Getting to Bond University Campus map Parking Close Home Job vacancy Jobs at Bond Professor / Associate Professor and Head of Discipline, Nutrition and Dietetics Start of main\n      content. Professor / Associate Professor and Head of Discipline, Nutrition and Dietetics Full-time, Continuing Appointment – Professor / Associate Professor and 5-year appointment as Head of Discipline Reference number: 201409623 About the position As Australia’s first private, not-for-profit university’, Bond University based in Robina on the Gold Coast seeks to be recognised internationally as a leading independent university, imbued with a spirit to innovate, a commitment to influence and a dedication to inspire tomorrow's professionals who share a personalised and transformational student experience. Champion academic excellence and growth in Nutrition & Dietetics at Bond University Inspire academic excellence and continue developing a high-performing team Drive program growth, research impact and industry engagement Join Australia’s top university for teaching* and enjoy staff benefits including: Free staff car parking Up to 18/26 weeks of parental leave# Salary packaging options for FBT and Non-FBT items# Annual leave loading for continuing and fixed term Academic staff Staff wellbeing program Free & Confidential Employee Assistance Program available for all staff Study assistance for staff and dependants# Corporate health and finance discounts Onsite Medical Centre and Counselling Services Onsite Sports Centre including gym, fitness classes and pool# About the Faculty and Discipline The Faculty of Health Sciences and Medicine is committed to developing professionals distinguished by excellence in  scientific and clinical practice, leadership, ethics, compassion and humanity. . The Faculty offers programs across  Biomedical Science, Exercise and Sports Science, Health Sciences, Healthcare Innovations, Medicine, Nutrition and Dietetics, Occupational Therapy and Physiotherapy. . The Faculty is recognised for its innovative approaches to health education and research and is home to leading  research centres including the internationally recognised Institute for Evidence-Based Healthcare . The Faculty’s facilities support contemporary education, research and clinical practice, and include the Bond University Health and Wellness Clinic , an interdisciplinary allied health clinic providing services to the community while supporting student placements. The Nutrition and Dietetics disciplines is a well-established and collaborative academic community with strengths across education, research and professional practice. The discipline delivers the Graduate Certificate and Graduate Diploma in Nutrition, and its flagship Master of Nutrition and Dietetics Practice, which is accredited by Dietitians Australia and the US Accreditation Council for Education in Nutrition and Dietetics. The Masters of Nutrition and Dietetics Practice integrates evidence-based learning with substantial professional practice and research experiences, including 24 weeks of professional practice internships and a 20-week research internship. The discipline brings together expertise across areas including public health nutrition, sports nutrition and applied nutrition research, and benefits from strong external partnerships and several conjoint appointments that strengthen connections with industry and professional practice. The Head of Discipline will provide academic leadership education, research and professional engagement, while continuing to build the discipline’s profile partnerships and impact. About the Position The Faculty of Health Sciences and Medicine is seeking an accomplished academic leader to lead its Nutrition and Dietetics discipline. This is an opportunity to provide strategic leadership for an established and highly regarded program, shaping its future direction and ensuring continued excellence in learning and teaching, research, accreditation and industry engagement. As Head of Discipline, you will work closely with Faculty leadership to drive program quality, student outcomes and sustainable growth. You will lead and mentor a talented academic team, fostering a collaborative, high-performing culture that supports innovation, professional development and academic excellence across teaching, research and professional practice. The role offers the opportunity to strengthen the profile and impact of Nutrition and Dietetics through research leadership, strategic partnerships and engagement with industry, healthcare providers, professional bodies and the broader community. As a key member of the Faculty leadership team, you will contribute to the ongoing success and reputation of the discipline and the University. The Head of Discipline role is a five-year appointment that may be renewed by mutual agreement. About the person We are seeking a respected academic leader with a passion for developing people, advancing the discipline and delivering outstanding educational and research outcomes. The ideal applicant will have the following: A PhD in Dietetics, Nutrition or a related discipline and current Accredited Practising Dietitian (APD) status, or eligibility to obtain and maintain APD status. Demonstrated success in academic leadership, including developing and mentoring academic staff and fostering a positive, collaborative culture. Significant experience leading accredited dietetics programs and driving continuous quality improvement. A strong research profile, including high-quality publications, research funding success and national and/or international recognition. Expertise in curriculum development, learning and teaching excellence, and contemporary educational practice. Experience building productive partnerships with industry, healthcare organisations and professional bodies. Demonstrated capability in strategic planning, resource management and contributing to organisational growth and success. You will bring the credibility, leadership capability and vision to inspire academic excellence, develop future leaders and strengthen the standing and impact of Nutrition and Dietetics at Bond University. Salary details The salary for this position is outlined below and will be negotiated commensurate with skills, qualifications, and experience. Bond University Academic Australian Public Sector Descriptor Salary (base) - Full-time Equivalent Professor Professor (Level E) $221,723.17 per annum* Associate Professor A Associate Professor (Level D) $189,734.53 per annum* *plus 12% superannuation Additional information For further details regarding this appointment, please reference the Position Descriptions and relevant Selection Criteria: Head of Discipline, Nutrition and Dietetics Position Description Professor Position Description Associate Professor A Position Description Bond University will be supported in its search for this appointment by the executive search firm, The Insight Group. For a confidential discussion about this opportunity or to apply, please contact Dr. Rohan Carr or Ms. Emily Witts at The Insight Group via [email protected] or by phone at +61 3 9654 3288. They can also provide a detailed Candidate Information Pack. Application and submission details Please submit your application, including a Resume and a Cover Letter addressing the Selection Criteria outlined in the Position Description directly via [email protected] . If you require any assistance with your application submission, please contact Dr. Rohan Carr or Ms Emily Witts at The Insight Group at [email protected] For current Bond University staff, apply directly via People Connect , log in with staff credentials, from the Home dashboard select Careers, select the role and apply. Applications close: 11:59 PM, Tuesday, 24 November 2026. Interviews will take place week commencing 7 December 2026. Applicants must have current work rights in Australia at the time of application. This status will be verified as part of the recruitment process. Pre-employment checks: Appointment is subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks (including working rights verification, reference checks and a certified copy of your highest qualification). In line with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence 2025, preferred candidates must complete a Gender-Based Violence (GBV) Declaration, and any offer of employment will be conditional upon the University’s review of the declaration."
    },
