ities Fee Bond Sports Centre Group exercise classes Personal training Sports Centre memberships Student housing options Student rights and responsibilities Complaints involving the behaviour of others Advocacy and support Appeals Your responsibilities Your rights Student conduct and misconduct Student surveys Graduate Outcomes Survey Student Experience Survey Opportunities Outbound student mobility Partnering with DFAT Exchange at Bond Participating institutions Asia Europe North America Information sessions Exchange blog How to apply Financial information and funding New Colombo Plan Scholarship 2027 Preparing to go Overseas Back at Bond Frequently asked questions Mooting at Bond What is mooting Mooting opportunities Mooting accolades Grants and scholarships Elite Athlete Fund Student Hardship Grant Student Opportunity Fund Frequently asked questions FinTech Hub training Bond Legal Clinics Program The Bond Law Clinic Climate Sustainability Clinic Criminal Law Clinic How to apply Internet Law Research Clinic My Community Legal Clinic Beyond Bond Graduation Preparing to graduate Conferral dates Ceremony information Ceremony videos Graduation booklets Graduation documents MyBond Library iLearn Staff iLearn Library Email Staff Intranet Online Service Catalogue Careers at Bond People Connect Alumni About Bond alumni Online Bond community The Arch Industry and partners Global education partners Sponsorship opportunities News and events News Events Contact Getting to Bond University Campus map Parking Close Home Job vacancy Jobs at Bond Accessibility & Inclusion Manager Start of main\n      content. Accessibility & Inclusion Manager Full-Time, Continuing Appointment Reference number: 201409541 About the position As Australia’s first private, not-for-profit university, Bond University based in Robina on the Gold Coast seeks to be recognised internationally as a leading independent university, imbued with a spirit to innovate, a commitment to influence and a dedication to inspire tomorrow's professionals who share a personalised and transformational student experience. Support Bond University’s strategic approach to accessibility and inclusion. Build capability and empower others to create genuinely inclusive study and work environments. Combine strategic leadership with specialist expertise, team leadership and complex student case management. Fantastic benefits package and great Gold Coast location Join Australia’s top university for teaching* and enjoy staff benefits including: Free staff car parking 36.75 hour standard work week Access to flexible work/work from home arrangements# Up to 18/26 weeks of parental leave# Salary packaging options for FBT and Non-FBT items# 17.5% of base salary leave loading Staff wellbeing program Free & Confidential Employee Assistance Program available for all staff Study assistance for staff and dependents# Corporate health and finance discounts Onsite Medical Centre and Counselling Services Onsite Sports Centre including gym, fitness classes and pool# About the Position The Accessibility and Inclusion Manager is a key leadership role responsible for strengthening accessibility, inclusion and equitable practice across Bond University. Leading the Accessibility & Inclusion function, the position coordinates implementation of the University’s Disability Inclusion and Accessibility Plan (DIAP), building shared ownership, capability and consistent inclusive practice across faculties, professional service areas and central teams. The role provides expert advice on complex and systemic accessibility and inclusion matters and works collaboratively with stakeholders across the University to translate strategy, legislation and best practice into meaningful action. A strong focus is placed on building the capability of staff and supporting the co-design of initiatives that create an accessible and inclusive study and work environment. The Manager leads and supports the Accessibility & Inclusion Advisor and oversees the quality and consistency of service delivery. Importantly, the position also maintains a direct connection with students through a caseload, complex case management and admission reviews, ensuring broader accessibility initiatives remain grounded in the lived experience and needs of Bond students. This is an opportunity to combine strategic leadership, specialist expertise and practical impact, helping to embed accessibility and inclusion as a shared responsibility across the University. About the person You will be an experienced accessibility and inclusion professional who can support Bond University’s strategic approach to accessibility and inclusion, build capability across the University, and empower others to create genuinely inclusive study and work environments. You will combine strategic thinking with specialist expertise, people leadership and confidence managing complex student accessibility matters. You will bring: A relevant tertiary qualification and strong experience in accessibility, disability, inclusion or equity, preferably within higher education. Experience leading and developing staff, including case consultation, workload management and professional development. Strong knowledge of disability and accessibility legislation, Universal Design for Learning (UDL), policy and contemporary sector practice. Expertise in complex student accessibility matters, including reasonable adjustments, inherent requirements, placements, complaints and appeals. Knowledge of neuroaffirming and trauma-informed approaches and their application to practice and service delivery. Strong communication, influencing and facilitation skills, with the ability to engage stakeholders, build capability and strengthen shared responsibility for inclusion. A strategic and evidence-informed approach to accessibility, risk, data and continuous improvement. If you are committed to making a meaningful difference and ensuring a more inclusive future for students and staff, we encourage you to apply for this vital role. Salary details The salary for the position commences at $116,195 per annum, plus 12% superannuation. Additional information Position-related enquiries can be directed to Stephanie Cooper, Head of Service, Student Counselling, Health & Wellbeing at [email protected] Application and submission details For further details regarding this appointment, please reference the Position Description and Selection Criteria Click Apply Now and Create New Account to get started. You can: Upload your Resume – your account will be created automatically, or Manually enter your details to set up your account. Please ensure your application includes: A current resume A cover letter addressing the Selection Criteria outlined in the Position Description above For current Bond University staff, apply directly via People Connect , log in with staff credentials, from the Home dashboard select Careers, select the role and apply. If you require any assistance with your application submission, please visit Applying for jobs at Bond . Applications close: 11:59pm, Monday 9 November 2026. Pre-employment checks: Appointment is subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks (including working rights verification, reference checks and a certified copy of your highest qualification). In line with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence 2025, preferred candidates must complete a Gender-Based Violence (GBV) Declaration, and any offer of employment will be conditional upon the University’s review of the declaration. For more information, please visit our website via this link: Applying for Jobs at Bond Conditions of employment are offered under a Bond Workplace Agreement (BWA). Bond University is an equal opportunity employer, and we encourage our students and staff to respect individuality, inclusiveness and diversity. In line with Bond University’s values, people from diverse backgrounds, women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, people who identify as LGBTIQ+, and people with a disability are encouraged to apply for positions at the University . Please advise the Talent Acquisition Team if you require any reasonable accommodations to assist you at anytime during the recruitment process. For more information, visit Supporting diversity at Bond | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Bond University Privacy Policy # Eligibility criteria or membership fees apply *Australian Financial Review’s Best Universities Ranking 2024 APPLY NOW Applications close: 9th November 2026 Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Read more about our acknowledgment of country Facebook LinkedIn Instagram TikTok YouTube Twitter WeChat Weibo Bond University Privacy Policy Disclaimer CRICOS Provider Code 00017B TEQSA Provider ID PRV12072"
    },
