culty of Law Faculty of Society & Design Transformation CoLab Academic calendar Census dates Manage your enrolment Subject finder Timetables Enrol in your subjects Changing your subjects Changing your program Withdrawing or taking a break Compassionate or compelling circumstances Withdrawal without penalty Cross institutional study Unique Student Identifier (USI) Fees and other costs Payment methods Transcripts and documents Assessment and grades Exams Assessment timetable Deferred exams Grades Review of results Academic integrity Academic misconduct and how to avoid it Generative Artificial Intelligence (Gen-AI) guide for students and staff Casual Room Bookings Services and support Bond Connect Academic Skills Centre Student Affairs and Service Quality Bond Business School Bond University College Attendance requirements Faculty of Health Sciences & Medicine Faculty of Law ​Indigenous student support Indigenous Student Success Program Nyombil Indigenous Support Centre International student support Medical and health services Student counselling Accessibility and inclusion Accessibility resources Feedback and questions University security Escape | Hide | Tell Emergency contacts Career Development Centre About the Career Development Centre Careers information for all our current students Employers and Industry Global experiences Graduates and alumni Verification of qualifications What's On Preventing and responding to gender-based violence Wellbeing services Student Wellbeing Advisors JP/Commissioner for Declarations service LGBTIQ+ services and support Campus life Bond University Student Association Student clubs Faculty Student Associations Bond University Business Students' Association Health and Sport Sciences Student Association (HSA) Medical Students Society of Bond University (MSSBU) Law Student Association Society & Design Student Association Club events Student events Students living on campus Sports Centre Smoke-free campus Merchandise Store Student Services and Amenities Fee Bond Sports Centre Group exercise classes Personal training Sports Centre memberships Student housing options Student rights and responsibilities Complaints involving the behaviour of others Advocacy and support Appeals Your responsibilities Your rights Student conduct and misconduct Student surveys Graduate Outcomes Survey Student Experience Survey Opportunities Outbound student mobility Partnering with DFAT Exchange at Bond Participating institutions Asia Europe North America Information sessions Exchange blog How to apply Financial information and funding New Colombo Plan Scholarship 2027 Preparing to go Overseas Back at Bond Frequently asked questions Mooting at Bond What is mooting Mooting opportunities Mooting accolades Grants and scholarships Elite Athlete Fund Student Hardship Grant Student Opportunity Fund Frequently asked questions FinTech Hub training Bond Legal Clinics Program The Bond Law Clinic Climate Sustainability Clinic Criminal Law Clinic How to apply Internet Law Research Clinic My Community Legal Clinic Beyond Bond Graduation Preparing to graduate Conferral dates Ceremony information Ceremony videos Graduation booklets Graduation documents MyBond Library iLearn Staff iLearn Library Email Staff Intranet Online Service Catalogue Careers at Bond People Connect Alumni About Bond alumni Online Bond community The Arch Industry and partners Global education partners Sponsorship opportunities News and events News Events Contact Getting to Bond University Campus map Parking Close Home Job vacancy Jobs at Bond Technical Assistant, Research Laboratories Start of main\n      content. Technical Assistant, Research Laboratories Full Time, Continuing Appointment Reference number: 201409299 About the position As Australia’s first private, not-for-profit university, Bond University based in Robina on the Gold Coast seeks to be recognised internationally as a leading independent university, imbued with a spirit to innovate, a commitment to influence and a dedication to inspire tomorrow's professionals who share a personalised and transformational student experience. Start your laboratory career in a practical role supporting day-to-day research activities. Gain hands-on experience across research laboratories and animal facilities. Work as part of a supportive technical team with training and guidance provided. Join Australia’s top university for teaching* and enjoy staff benefits including: Free staff car parking 36.75 hour standard work week Access to flexible work/work from home arrangements# Up to 18/26 weeks of parental leave# Salary packaging options for FBT and Non-FBT items# 17.5% of base salary leave loading Staff wellbeing program Free & Confidential Employee Assistance Program available for all staff Study assistance for staff and dependents# Corporate health and finance discounts Onsite Medical Centre and Counselling Services Onsite Sports Centre including gym, fitness classes and pool# As Technical Assistant, Research Laboratories, you will provide practical support across Bond’s research laboratories and animal facilities. Under guidance, you will assist with tasks such as animal care, laboratory preparation, cleaning and sterilisation, stock control and basic equipment checks. You will follow established procedures and work closely with technical staff to help keep the facilities operating safely and efficiently. About the person You are reliable, practical and willing to learn. You enjoy hands-on work, follow instructions carefully and take pride in completing routine tasks accurately. You work well as part of a team and understand the importance of safety, cleanliness and animal welfare. This role may suit someone beginning their career in a laboratory, animal care or technical support environment. Relevant study or practical experience would be helpful, but training and guidance will be provided. As animal welfare is central to the role, you must be willing to participate in weekend and out-of-hours animal care duties. The ideal candidate will bring: A reliable and practical approach to completing routine tasks. The ability to follow instructions and established procedures carefully. Good organisation and attention to detail. Clear communication skills and a willingness to work as part of a team. An interest in laboratory or animal care work and a commitment to safety and animal welfare. Salary details The salary for the position commences at $66,615.31 per annum, plus 12% superannuation Additional information Position-related enquiries can be directed to Dr. Katie Powell (Manager, Research Laboratories) at [email protected] or 07 5595 1236 Application and submission details For further details regarding this appointment, please reference the Position Description and Selection Criteria . Click Apply Now and Create New Account to get started. You can: Upload your Resume – your account will be created automatically, or Manually enter your details to set up your account. Please ensure your application includes: A current resume A cover letter addressing the Selection Criteria outlined in the Position Description above For current Bond University staff, apply directly via HR Connect , log in with staff credentials, from the Home dashboard select Careers, select the role and apply. If you require any assistance with your application submission, please visit Applying for jobs at Bond . Applications close: 11:59pm on Sunday 15 November 2026. Applicants must have current work rights in Australia at the time of application. This status will be verified as part of the recruitment process. Pre-employment checks: Appointment is subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks (including working rights verification, reference checks and a certified copy of your highest qualification). In line with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence 2025, preferred candidates must complete a Gender-Based Violence (GBV) Declaration, and any offer of employment will be conditional upon the University’s review of the declaration. For more information, please visit our website via this link: Applying for Jobs at Bond Conditions of employment are offered under a Bond Workplace Agreement (BWA). Bond University is an equal opportunity employer, and we encourage our students and staff to respect individuality, inclusiveness and diversity. In line with Bond University’s values, people from diverse backgrounds, women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, people who identify as LGBTIQ+, and people with a disability are encouraged to apply for positions at the University . Please advise the Talent Acquisition Team if you require any reasonable accommodations to assist you at anytime during the recruitment process. For more information, visit Supporting diversity at Bond | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Bond University Privacy Policy # Eligibility criteria or membership fees apply *Australian Financial Review’s Best Universities Ranking 2024 APPLY NOW Applications close: 15th November 2026 Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Read more about our acknowledgment of country Facebook LinkedIn Instagram TikTok YouTube Twitter WeChat Weibo Bond University Privacy Policy Disclaimer CRICOS Provider Code 00017B TEQSA Provider ID PRV12072"
    },
