nt Services and Amenities Fee Bond Sports Centre Group exercise classes Personal training Sports Centre memberships Student housing options Student rights and responsibilities Complaints involving the behaviour of others Advocacy and support Appeals Your responsibilities Your rights Student conduct and misconduct Student surveys Graduate Outcomes Survey Student Experience Survey Opportunities Outbound student mobility Partnering with DFAT Exchange at Bond Participating institutions Asia Europe North America Information sessions Exchange blog How to apply Financial information and funding New Colombo Plan Scholarship 2027 Preparing to go Overseas Back at Bond Frequently asked questions Mooting at Bond What is mooting Mooting opportunities Mooting accolades Grants and scholarships Elite Athlete Fund Student Hardship Grant Student Opportunity Fund Frequently asked questions FinTech Hub training Bond Legal Clinics Program The Bond Law Clinic Climate Sustainability Clinic Criminal Law Clinic How to apply Internet Law Research Clinic My Community Legal Clinic Beyond Bond Graduation Preparing to graduate Conferral dates Ceremony information Ceremony videos Graduation booklets Graduation documents MyBond Library iLearn Staff iLearn Library Email Staff Intranet Online Service Catalogue Careers at Bond People Connect Alumni About Bond alumni Online Bond community The Arch Industry and partners Global education partners Sponsorship opportunities News and events News Events Contact Getting to Bond University Campus map Parking Close Home Job vacancy Jobs at Bond Technical Officer, Bond Institute of Health and Sport Start of main\n      content. Technical Officer, Bond Institute of Health and Sport Full-Time, Continuing Appointment Reference number: 201411277 About the position As Australia’s first private, not-for-profit university, Bond University based in Robina on the Gold Coast seeks to be recognised internationally as a leading independent university, imbued with a spirit to innovate, a commitment to influence and a dedication to inspire tomorrow's professionals who share a personalised and transformational student experience. Play a hands-on role in delivering practical learning experiences for Bond’s health students. Gain broad technical experience in a varied role supporting practical teaching across the health disciplines. Join at an exciting time and help establish practical teaching for Bond’s new Exercise Physiology and Speech Pathology programs Join Australia’s top university for teaching* and enjoy staff benefits including: Free staff car parking 36.75 hour standard work week Access to flexible work/work from home arrangements# Up to 18/26 weeks of parental leave# Salary packaging options for FBT and Non-FBT items# 17.5% of base salary leave loading Staff wellbeing program Free & Confidential Employee Assistance Program available for all staff Study assistance for staff and dependents# Corporate health and finance discounts Onsite Medical Centre and Counselling Services Onsite Sports Centre including gym, fitness classes and pool# If you enjoy practical work, solving problems and being part of the action, this role offers the chance to make a visible difference to how students learn. You will help turn teaching plans into well-run practical sessions by preparing spaces and equipment, supporting staff and students, and making sure everything is ready when it matters. Based at the Bond Institute of Health and Sport, you will support practical learning across Exercise Science, Occupational Therapy, Physiotherapy, Nutrition and Dietetics, Medicine and other health disciplines. One day you may be setting up equipment for an Exercise Science or physiotherapy class, the next preparing resources for nutrition, medicine or occupational therapy. You will also join at an exciting time, helping build the technical support, equipment and practical teaching capability behind Bond’s two new programs in Exercise Physiology and Speech Pathology. About the person This role would suit a recent graduate in allied health, Exercise and Sport Science or a related discipline who is interested in applying their knowledge in a practical university environment. The successful candidate will be organised, adaptable and willing to develop their technical capability across a range of health disciplines. They will bring a hands-on approach, sound judgement and a genuine commitment to supporting students, academic staff and colleagues. Key attributes include: A qualification in allied health, health science, exercise and sport science or a related area, or an equivalent combination of education and relevant practical experience. A practical mindset and confidence getting involved, learning equipment and working through problems as they arise. Strong organisation and attention to detail, particularly when preparing multiple classes, equipment and resources. A calm, helpful approach and the confidence to work with students, academics and technical colleagues. The ability to follow safe work practices, instructions and procedures while knowing when to ask for help or escalate an issue. Good digital skills and the ability to keep clear, accurate records. Flexibility and curiosity, with a willingness to work across different health disciplines and adapt when priorities change. A current driver licence and willingness to travel between campuses Salary details The salary for the position commences at $76,152.44 per annum, plus 12% superannuation. Additional information Position-related enquiries can be directed to Kristin Bower, Senior Technical Officer on 0448 856 494 or email [email protected] Application and submission details For further details regarding this appointment, please reference the Position Description and Selection Criteria Click Apply Now and Create New Account to get started. You can: Upload your Resume – your account will be created automatically, or Manually enter your details to set up your account. Please ensure your application includes: A current resume A cover letter addressing the Selection Criteria outlined in the Position Description above For current Bond University staff, apply directly via People Connect , log in with staff credentials, from the Home dashboard select Careers, select the role and apply. If you require any assistance with your application submission, please visit Applying for jobs at Bond . Applications close: 11:59pm, Sunday 15 th November 2026. Applicants must have current work rights in Australia at the time of application. This status will be verified as part of the recruitment process. Pre-employment checks: Appointment is subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks (including working rights verification, reference checks and a certified copy of your highest qualification). In line with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence 2025, preferred candidates must complete a Gender-Based Violence (GBV) Declaration, and any offer of employment will be conditional upon the University’s review of the declaration. For more information, please visit our website via this link: Applying for Jobs at Bond Conditions of employment are offered under a Bond Workplace Agreement (BWA). Bond University is an equal opportunity employer, and we encourage our students and staff to respect individuality, inclusiveness and diversity. In line with Bond University’s values, people from diverse backgrounds, women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, people who identify as LGBTIQ+, and people with a disability are encouraged to apply for positions at the University . Please advise the Talent Acquisition Team if you require any reasonable accommodations to assist you at anytime during the recruitment process. For more information, visit Supporting diversity at Bond | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Bond University Privacy Policy # Eligibility criteria or membership fees apply *Australian Financial Review’s Best Universities Ranking 2024 APPLY NOW Applications close: 15th November 2026 Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Read more about our acknowledgment of country Facebook LinkedIn Instagram TikTok YouTube Twitter WeChat Weibo Bond University Privacy Policy Disclaimer CRICOS Provider Code 00017B TEQSA Provider ID PRV12072"
