 Services and Amenities Fee Bond Sports Centre Group exercise classes Personal training Sports Centre memberships Student housing options Student rights and responsibilities Complaints involving the behaviour of others Advocacy and support Appeals Your responsibilities Your rights Student conduct and misconduct Student surveys Graduate Outcomes Survey Student Experience Survey Opportunities Outbound student mobility Partnering with DFAT Exchange at Bond Participating institutions Asia Europe North America Information sessions Exchange blog How to apply Financial information and funding New Colombo Plan Scholarship 2027 Preparing to go Overseas Back at Bond Frequently asked questions Mooting at Bond What is mooting Mooting opportunities Mooting accolades Grants and scholarships Elite Athlete Fund Student Hardship Grant Student Opportunity Fund Frequently asked questions FinTech Hub training Bond Legal Clinics Program The Bond Law Clinic Climate Sustainability Clinic Criminal Law Clinic How to apply Internet Law Research Clinic My Community Legal Clinic Beyond Bond Graduation Preparing to graduate Conferral dates Ceremony information Ceremony videos Graduation booklets Graduation documents MyBond Library iLearn Staff iLearn Library Email Staff Intranet Online Service Catalogue Careers at Bond People Connect Alumni About Bond alumni Online Bond community The Arch Industry and partners Global education partners Sponsorship opportunities News and events News Events Contact Getting to Bond University Campus map Parking Close Home Job vacancy Jobs at Bond Domestic Student Recruitment Manager (Sydney-based) Start of main\n      content. Domestic Student Recruitment Manager (Sydney-based) Full-time, Continuing Appointment Reference number: 201402508 About the position As Australia’s first private, not-for-profit university, Bond University based in Robina on the Gold Coast seeks to be recognised internationally as a leading independent university, imbued with a spirit to innovate, a commitment to influence and a dedication to inspire tomorrow's professionals who share a personalised and transformational student experience. Join a university with a strong commitment to student success and retention Leave a lasting impact on the university's growth and success Enjoy a dynamic working environment and great staff benefits Join Australia’s top university for teaching* and enjoy staff benefits including: 36.75 hour standard work week Up to 18/26 weeks of parental leave# Salary packaging options for FBT and Non-FBT items# 17.5% of base salary leave loading Staff wellbeing program Free & Confidential Employee Assistance Program available for all staff Study assistance for staff and dependents# Corporate health and finance discounts Free staff car parking (if based on main campus) Onsite Medical Centre and Counselling Services (if based on main campus) Onsite Sports Centre including gym, fitness classes and pool# (if based on main campus) About the Position The Office of Future Students are seeking a dynamic individual for Domestic Student Recruitment manager based in Sydney, who will be instrumental in driving enrolment objectives for both undergraduate and graduate programs. As a key member of the team, you will develop and execute innovative student recruitment strategies, with a focus on generating leads and building strong relationships across key domestic markets. You will play an important role in promoting Bond University, strengthening our presence in the market and contributing to enrolment growth. Responsibilities will include: Developing and implementing strategic and operational plans to support domestic student recruitment. Driving lead generation and representing and promoting Bond University across key markets. Building and maintaining strong relationships with prospective students, schools, industry partners and internal and external stakeholders. Understanding and promoting Bond’s pathway programs and academic offerings. Using market insights and data to identify opportunities and inform recruitment activity. Delivering exceptional service to prospective students and university stakeholders. Location of Position This position is primarily based in Sydney. Candidates may also be based at Bond University's Gold Coast campus, with regular monthly travel to Sydney required. The role involves regular travel within Sydney, occasional travel to other locations, and may require work outside standard business hours. About the person The ideal applicant will have: Tertiary qualifications in business, commerce, marketing, education or a related discipline, together with experience in business development, sales, student recruitment or a related field. Demonstrated experience developing and implementing recruitment, business development or sales strategies, with a strong focus on achieving results. Strong skills in lead generation, consultative selling and relationship management. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including confidence presenting to a range of audiences. Demonstrated ability to use data and market insights to identify opportunities and inform decision-making. An understanding of the Australian tertiary education sector and the domestic student recruitment landscape. Applicants must hold, or be able to obtain, a current Blue Card or equivalent in NSW. Salary details The salary range for this full-time position is $116,195 to $133,179 per annum, dependent on skills, qualifications and experience, plus 17.5% superannuation. Additional information Position-related enquiries can be directed to Julia Nguyen, Domestic Student Recruitment Manager at [email protected] on behalf of Jit Loh, Director - Domestic Recruitment Application and submission details For further details regarding this appointment, please reference the Position Description and Selection Criteria Click Apply Now and Create New Account to get started. You can: Upload your Resume – your account will be created automatically, or Manually enter your details to set up your account. Please ensure your application includes: A current resume A cover letter addressing the Selection Criteria outlined in the Position Description above For current Bond University staff, apply directly via People Connect , log in with staff credentials, from the Home dashboard select Careers, select the role and apply.If you require any assistance with your application submission, please visit Applying for jobs at Bond . Applications close: 11:59pm, Sunday, 22 November 2026 Interviews will be conducted on Monday, 30 November 2026 Pre-employment checks: Appointment is subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks (including working rights verification, reference checks and a certified copy of your highest qualification). In line with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence 2025, preferred candidates must complete a Gender-Based Violence (GBV) Declaration, and any offer of employment will be conditional upon the University’s review of the declaration. For more information, please visit our website via this link: Applying for Jobs at Bond Conditions of employment are offered under a Bond Workplace Agreement (BWA). Bond University is an equal opportunity employer, and we encourage our students and staff to respect individuality, inclusiveness and diversity.  In line with Bond University’s values, people from diverse backgrounds, women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, people who identify as LGBTIQ+, and people with a disability are encouraged to apply for positions at the University . Please advise the Talent Acquisition Team if you require any reasonable accommodations to assist you at anytime during the recruitment process. For more information, visit Supporting diversity at Bond | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Bond University Privacy Policy # Eligibility criteria or membership fees apply *Australian Financial Review’s Best Universities Ranking 2024 APPLY NOW Applications close: 22nd November 2026 Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Read more about our acknowledgment of country Facebook LinkedIn Instagram TikTok YouTube Twitter WeChat Weibo Bond University Privacy Policy Disclaimer CRICOS Provider Code 00017B TEQSA Provider ID PRV12072"
    },
