 Services and Amenities Fee Bond Sports Centre Group exercise classes Personal training Sports Centre memberships Student housing options Student rights and responsibilities Complaints involving the behaviour of others Advocacy and support Appeals Your responsibilities Your rights Student conduct and misconduct Student surveys Graduate Outcomes Survey Student Experience Survey Opportunities Outbound student mobility Partnering with DFAT Exchange at Bond Participating institutions Asia Europe North America Information sessions Exchange blog How to apply Financial information and funding New Colombo Plan Scholarship 2027 Preparing to go Overseas Back at Bond Frequently asked questions Mooting at Bond What is mooting Mooting opportunities Application procedure Mooting accolades Grants and scholarships Elite Athlete Fund Student Hardship Grant Student Opportunity Fund Frequently asked questions FinTech Hub training Bond Legal Clinics Program The Bond Law Clinic Climate Sustainability Clinic Criminal Law Clinic How to apply Internet Law Research Clinic My Community Legal Clinic Beyond Bond Graduation Preparing to graduate Conferral dates Ceremony information Ceremony videos Graduation booklets Graduation documents MyBond Library iLearn Staff iLearn Library Email Staff Intranet Online Service Catalogue Careers at Bond People Connect Alumni About Bond alumni Online Bond community The Arch Industry and partners Global education partners Sponsorship opportunities News and events News Events Contact Getting to Bond University Campus map Parking Close Home Job vacancy Jobs at Bond First Nations Simulated Participants (Multiple Positions) Start of main\n      content. First Nations Simulated Participants (Multiple Positions) Casual Appointment Reference number: 134331786 About the position As Australia’s first private not-for-profit university, Bond University has earned an international reputation as a leading independent university. Imbued with a spirit to innovate, a commitment to influence and a dedication to inspire tomorrow’s professionals, Bond offers a personalised, transformational and deliberately different student experience. Join a dynamic and supportive team dedicated to excellence in higher education Build relationships with students, faculty, and staff across campus Central and vibrant Robina based campus with free parking Join Australia’s top university for teaching* and enjoy staff benefits including: Free staff car parking Staff wellbeing program Onsite Medical Centre and Counselling Services Onsite Sports Centre including gym, fitness classes and pool# This is an Aboriginal/Torres Strait Islander identified position which is a genuine occupational qualification and is authorised under section 14(d) of the Anti-Discrimination Act 1977. Bond University Faculty of Health Sciences and Medicine provides education to students in health degrees including Medicine, Physiotherapy, Nutrition and Dietetics and Occupational Therapy. Bond has a personalised teaching model with emphasis on providing small class sizes as often as possible, and for clinical students this may be in a “simulated” or “role play” environment where students can learn or demonstrate a skill. A Simulated Participant is a well staff member who portrays a patient (simulated patient), family member or client to meet the objectives of the simulation. Simulated Participants engage in providing feedback to the learner. Simulated Participants will partner with various programs in teaching for a variety of educational activities. The names of these activities reflect the level of involvement and training required, such as History Taking or Physical Examination Skills. The Faculty of Health Sciences and Medicine welcomes applications for the position of Simulated Participant within the Faculty of Health Sciences and Medicine, who will be an integral member of the team. About the person The successful candidate will: Identify as Aboriginal/Torres Strait Islander Have the ability to act in a culturally appropriate and respectful manner. Demonstrate a high level of communication skills and a positive attitude Demonstrate performance skills to the requirements of the simulation Give quality feedback to student health professionals as directed by the tutor Show ability to build positive relationships with diverse teams Commitment to the Bond University Strategic Plan Previous experience as a Simulated Participant or in simulated settings is favourable. Salary details The hourly rate for this position is $49.70 (inclusive of 25% casual loading) plus 12% superannuation per annum. Additional information Position related enquiries can be directed to Dr Jessica Stokes-Parish, Simulated Participant Program Academic Lead, at [email protected] Application and submission details For further details regarding this appointment, please reference the Position Description and Selection Criteria. Click Apply Now and Create New Account to get started. You can: Upload your Resume – your account will be created automatically, or Manually enter your details to set up your account. Please ensure your application includes: A current resume A cover letter addressing the Selection Criteria outlined in the Position Description above For current Bond University staff, apply directly via HR Connect , log in with staff credentials, from the Home dashboard select Careers, select the role and apply. If you require any assistance with your application submission, please visit Applying for jobs at Bond . Applications close: 11:59 PM, 31 December 2026. This is an Identified position . Applicants must identify as Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander. As part of the recruitment process, you will be asked to provide a Certificate of Aboriginality , or other documentation confirming your identity from a recognised community organisation. Conditions of employment are offered under a Bond Workplace Agreement (BWA). Bond University is an equal opportunity employer, and we encourage our students and staff to respect individuality and diversity. In line with Bond University’s values, people from diverse backgrounds, women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, people who identify as LGBTIQ+, and people with a disability are encouraged to apply for positions at the University. Bond University Privacy Policy # Eligibility criteria or membership fees apply *Australian Financial Review’s Best Universities Ranking 2024 APPLY NOW Applications close: 31st December 2026 Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Read more about our acknowledgment of country Facebook LinkedIn Instagram TikTok YouTube Twitter WeChat Weibo Bond University Privacy Policy Disclaimer CRICOS Provider Code 00017B TEQSA Provider ID PRV12072"
