Centre Group exercise classes Personal training Sports Centre memberships Student housing options Student rights and responsibilities Complaints involving the behaviour of others Advocacy and support Appeals Your responsibilities Your rights Student conduct and misconduct Student surveys Graduate Outcomes Survey Student Experience Survey Opportunities Outbound student mobility Partnering with DFAT Exchange at Bond Participating institutions Asia Europe North America Information sessions Exchange blog How to apply Financial information and funding New Colombo Plan Scholarship 2027 Preparing to go Overseas Back at Bond Frequently asked questions Mooting at Bond What is mooting Mooting opportunities Mooting accolades Grants and scholarships Elite Athlete Fund Student Hardship Grant Student Opportunity Fund Frequently asked questions FinTech Hub training Bond Legal Clinics Program The Bond Law Clinic Climate Sustainability Clinic Criminal Law Clinic How to apply Internet Law Research Clinic My Community Legal Clinic Beyond Bond Graduation Preparing to graduate Conferral dates Ceremony information Ceremony videos Graduation booklets Graduation documents MyBond Library iLearn Staff iLearn Library Email Staff Intranet Online Service Catalogue Careers at Bond People Connect Alumni About Bond alumni Online Bond community The Arch Industry and partners Global education partners Sponsorship opportunities News and events News Events Contact Getting to Bond University Campus map Parking Close Home Job vacancy Jobs at Bond Storeperson Start of main\n      content. Storeperson Casual Appointment Reference number: 201411983 About the position As Australia’s first private, not-for-profit university’, Bond University based in Robina on the Gold Coast seeks to be recognised internationally as a leading independent university, imbued with a spirit to innovate, a commitment to influence and a dedication to inspire tomorrow's professionals who share a personalised and transformational student experience. Join Australia’s top university for teaching* and enjoy staff benefits including: Free staff car parking Staff wellbeing program Free & Confidential Employee Assistance Program available for all staff Corporate health and finance discounts Onsite Medical Centre and Counselling Services Onsite Sports Centre including gym, fitness classes and pool# Bond University is seeking an enthusiastic and reliable casual Storeperson to join the Food & Beverage team. This role plays an important part in supporting the smooth day-to-day operation of campus hospitality services through the efficient receipt, storage and distribution of goods across Food & Beverage outlets. The successful candidate will be a motivated, hands-on individual who takes pride in maintaining organised and accurate stock areas, rotating stock, and ensuring deliveries are received and stored correctly. With a strong focus on safety, hygiene and efficient stock management, you will contribute to the seamless operation of the team while working collaboratively with colleagues across Food & Beverage services. About the person You’re a reliable, organised and proactive team member who enjoys working in a practical, fast-paced environment. You take pride in keeping stock areas clean and well organised, can safely handle and move goods, and follow stock rotation, food safety and workplace procedures. Experience operating a walkie stacker/pedestrian forklift is desirable, while previous forklift experience and/or a current forklift licence will be highly regarded. You communicate well, work effectively as part of a team, and are willing to assist wherever needed to support the smooth operation of Food & Beverage services. You will need to have reliable availability to work between 7:00 am and 3:00 pm, Monday to Friday. Salary details The hourly rate for this casual role is $37.60 (includes 25% casual Loading) plus 12% superannuation. Additional information Position-related enquiries can be directed to Position-related enquiries can be directed to Stephen Walsh, Stores Manager at [email protected] Application and submission details For further details regarding this appointment, please reference the Position Description and Selection Criteria. Click Apply Now and Create New Account to get started. You can: Upload your Resume – your account will be created automatically, or Manually enter your details to set up your account. Please ensure your application includes: A current resume A cover letter addressing the Selection Criteria outlined in the Position Description above For current Bond University staff, apply directly via HR Connect , log in with staff credentials, from the Home dashboard select Careers, select the role and apply. If you require any assistance with your application submission, please visit Applying for jobs at Bond . Applications close: 11:59pm, Tuesday 17th November 2026. Pre-employment checks: Appointment is subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks (including working rights verification, reference checks and a certified copy of your highest qualification). In line with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence 2025, preferred candidates must complete a Gender-Based Violence (GBV) Declaration, and any offer of employment will be conditional upon the University’s review of the declaration. For more information, please visit our website via this link: Applying for Jobs at Bond. Conditions of employment are offered under a Bond Workplace Agreement (BWA). Bond University is an equal opportunity employer, and we encourage our students and staff to respect individuality, inclusiveness and diversity. In line with Bond University’s values, people from diverse backgrounds, women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, people who identify as LGBTIQ+, and people with a disability are encouraged to apply for positions at the University . Please advise the Talent Acquisition Team if you require any reasonable accommodations to assist you at anytime during the recruitment process. For more information, visit Supporting diversity at Bond | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Bond University Privacy Policy # Eligibility criteria or membership fees apply *Australian Financial Review’s Best Universities Ranking 2024 APPLY NOW Applications close: 17th November 2026 Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Read more about our acknowledgment of country Facebook LinkedIn Instagram TikTok YouTube Twitter WeChat Weibo Bond University Privacy Policy Disclaimer CRICOS Provider Code 00017B TEQSA Provider ID PRV12072"
