Amenities Fee Bond Sports Centre Group exercise classes Personal training Sports Centre memberships Student housing options Student rights and responsibilities Complaints involving the behaviour of others Advocacy and support Appeals Your responsibilities Your rights Student conduct and misconduct Student surveys Graduate Outcomes Survey Student Experience Survey Opportunities Outbound student mobility Partnering with DFAT Exchange at Bond Participating institutions Asia Europe North America Information sessions Exchange blog How to apply Financial information and funding New Colombo Plan Scholarship 2027 Preparing to go Overseas Back at Bond Frequently asked questions Mooting at Bond What is mooting Mooting opportunities Mooting accolades Grants and scholarships Elite Athlete Fund Student Hardship Grant Student Opportunity Fund Frequently asked questions FinTech Hub training Bond Legal Clinics Program The Bond Law Clinic Climate Sustainability Clinic Criminal Law Clinic How to apply Internet Law Research Clinic My Community Legal Clinic Beyond Bond Graduation Preparing to graduate Conferral dates Ceremony information Ceremony videos Graduation booklets Graduation documents MyBond Library iLearn Staff iLearn Library Email Staff Intranet Online Service Catalogue Careers at Bond People Connect Alumni About Bond alumni Online Bond community The Arch Industry and partners Global education partners Sponsorship opportunities News and events News Events Contact Getting to Bond University Campus map Parking Close Home Job vacancy Jobs at Bond Director, Office of Research Services Start of main\n      content. Director, Office of Research Services Full-time, 5-year appointment Reference number: 201415492 About the position As Australia’s first private, not-for-profit university’, Bond University based in Robina on the Gold Coast seeks to be recognised internationally as a leading independent university, imbued with a spirit to innovate, a commitment to influence and a dedication to inspire tomorrow's professionals who share a personalised and transformational student experience. Play a pivotal role in strengthening Bond’s national and international research reputation Support the Deputy Provost Research to advance Bond’s research strategy Develop strategies and initiatives in an ambitious, growing research culture Director, Office of Research Services Office of the Provost Full-time, 5-year appointment Position Reference Nr.: 201415492 Join Australia’s top university for teaching* and enjoy staff benefits including: Free staff car parking Salary packaging options for FBT and Non-FBT items# Staff wellbeing program Free & Confidential Employee Assistance Program available for all staff Study assistance for staff and dependants# Corporate health and finance discounts Onsite Medical Centre and Counselling Services Onsite Sports Centre including gym, fitness classes and pool# About the Office of Research Services The Office of Research Services plays a central role in enabling Bond University’s research ambition, providing the institutional infrastructure, governance and expertise that underpin research performance and impact. Situated within the Office of the Provost and working closely with the Deputy Provost Research, the Office connects University research strategy with its implementation across academic and professional portfolios. Its remit extends across research strategy and policy, external funding, research governance and compliance, financial management, research systems and statutory reporting, intellectual property and commercialisation. The Office works across the University and with government, funding bodies and industry to strengthen research capability, support researchers and ensure Bond University is well positioned within an evolving national and international research environment. About the Position The Director, Office of Research Services is a senior leadership opportunity to support the Deputy Provost Research in implementing and advancing Bond University’s research strategy, governance and external impact. Reporting directly to the Deputy Provost Research, the Director will provide authoritative advice to researchers and senior executives and help foster a University-wide culture of research innovation, excellence and accountability. With a University-wide remit, the Director will lead the Office of Research Services team in coordinating policy implementation, research systems, financial management, reporting and administrative infrastructure across the research portfolio. The Director will support the Deputy Provost Research in advancing external funding, intellectual property management and commercialisation initiatives, and will be responsible for meeting the University’s statutory reporting and compliance obligations, including safeguarding research data integrity. A key focus will be developing strategies and initiatives that strengthen the environment in which research can flourish and position the University to respond effectively to developments across the national and international research landscape. This role operates across academic, professional and external stakeholder communities. The Director will build productive relationships with senior University leaders, government agencies, research funding bodies and industry, while leading a high-performing professional team that enables researchers to pursue opportunities, navigate complexity and deliver research with impact. About the person You will be an accomplished leader in research management and strategy, bringing experience from complex university or research settings and the judgement, credibility and stakeholder engagement skills to advise and support the Deputy Provost Research. The ideal applicant will have the following: A relevant postgraduate qualification and significant senior-level experience in research management. Demonstrated success shaping and delivering research strategy, governance and institutional priorities. Strong executive advisory, influencing and stakeholder engagement capability across academic, government and industry environments. A proven ability to lead high-performing teams and translate strategy into measurable outcomes. Strong commercial and financial acumen, with experience across research funding, intellectual property and commercialisation. Exceptional communication and negotiation skills, with the ability to navigate complex and sensitive matters. This is an opportunity for a strategic and collaborative leader to work alongside the Deputy Provost Research and play a key role in advancing Bond University’s research performance, capability and impact. Salary details The salary will be negotiated and commensurate with skills and experience and be fully competitive in the Australian market.  Salary packaging options are available for eligible employees. Additional information Position-related enquiries can be directed to Professor Michael Kimlin, Deputy Provost, Research at [email protected] . Application and submission details For further details regarding this appointment, please reference the Position Description and Selection Criteria. Click Apply Now and Create New Account to get started. You can: Upload your Resume – your account will be created automatically, or Manually enter your details to set up your account. Please ensure your application includes: A current resume A cover letter addressing the Essential Attributes outlined in the Position Description in the Candidate Booklet. For current Bond University staff, apply directly via People Connect , log in with staff credentials, from the Home dashboard select Careers, select the role and apply. If you require any assistance with your application submission, please visit Applying for jobs at Bond . Applications close: 11:59pm, Thursday, 26 November 2026. Applicants must have current work rights in Australia at the time of application. This status will be verified as part of the recruitment process. Pre-employment checks: Appointment is subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks (including working rights verification, reference checks and a certified copy of your highest qualification). In line with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence 2025, preferred candidates must complete a Gender-Based Violence (GBV) Declaration, and any offer of employment will be conditional upon the University’s review of the declaration. For more information, please visit our website via this link: Applying for Jobs at Bond Bond University is an equal opportunity employer, and we encourage our students and staff to respect individuality, inclusiveness and diversity.  In line with Bond University’s values, people from diverse backgrounds, women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, people who identify as LGBTIQ+, and people with a disability are encouraged to apply for positions at the University . Please advise the Talent Acquisition Team if you require any reasonable accommodations to assist you at any time during the recruitment process. For more information, visit Supporting diversity at Bond | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Bond University Privacy Policy # Eligibility criteria or membership fees apply *Australian Financial Review’s Best Universities Ranking 2024 APPLY NOW Applications close: 26th November 2026 Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now sta"
