ces and Amenities Fee Bond Sports Centre Group exercise classes Personal training Sports Centre memberships Student housing options Student rights and responsibilities Complaints involving the behaviour of others Advocacy and support Appeals Your responsibilities Your rights Student conduct and misconduct Student surveys Graduate Outcomes Survey Student Experience Survey Opportunities Outbound student mobility Partnering with DFAT Exchange at Bond Participating institutions Asia Europe North America Information sessions Exchange blog How to apply Financial information and funding New Colombo Plan Scholarship 2027 Preparing to go Overseas Back at Bond Frequently asked questions Mooting at Bond What is mooting Mooting opportunities Mooting accolades Grants and scholarships Elite Athlete Fund Student Hardship Grant Student Opportunity Fund Frequently asked questions FinTech Hub training Bond Legal Clinics Program The Bond Law Clinic Climate Sustainability Clinic Criminal Law Clinic How to apply Internet Law Research Clinic My Community Legal Clinic Beyond Bond Graduation Preparing to graduate Conferral dates Ceremony information Ceremony videos Graduation booklets Graduation documents MyBond Library iLearn Staff iLearn Library Email Staff Intranet Online Service Catalogue Careers at Bond People Connect Alumni About Bond alumni Online Bond community The Arch Industry and partners Global education partners Sponsorship opportunities News and events News Events Contact Getting to Bond University Campus map Parking Close Home Job vacancy Jobs at Bond Manager, Applications and Process Improvement Start of main\n      content. Manager, Applications and Process Improvement Full-time, Continuing Appointment Reference number: 201413249 About the position As Australia's first private University, Bond University based at Robina, Gold Coast seeks to be recognised internationally as a leading independent university, imbued with a spirit to innovate, a commitment to influence and a dedication to inspire tomorrow's professionals who share a personalised and transformational student experience. Oversee university systems for student administration and records management. Drive student system and process improvements for top service and performance. Work with stakeholders to deliver an exceptional digital student experience. Join Australia’s number one University for teaching*, and enjoy staff benefits including: Free staff car parking Salary packaging options for FBT and Non-FBT items# 17.5% of base salary leave loading Staff wellbeing program Free & Confidential Employee Assistance Program available for all staff Study assistance for staff and dependents# Corporate health and finance discounts Onsite Medical Centre and Counselling Services Onsite Sports Centre including gym, fitness classes and pool# About the Position The Manager, Applications and Process Improvement is focused on delivering services to support the University’s commitment to an exceptional student experience, leading to positive outcomes in student success, retention and completion. The role will have a focus on student systems and associated process improvements, using an evidence-based approach to facilitate the identification and implementation of improvements as well as methods to measure service performance, implementation, and development. The post holder ensures consistency, smooth integration of systems and services, liaising with relevant internal and external stakeholders and effective management of change impacts. This includes identifying and investigating business process improvement opportunities and service delivery enhancements, coordinating the development and implementation of service improvement plans for specific systems or processes, in consultation with stakeholders and with the Director’s oversight. The post holder assists with implementing improvements to the university’s student system ( Student One ) in collaboration with the Manager, Student Systems & Data, and oversees management of applications such as the MyBond student portal and app, as well as systems support for Time Edit timetabling software. About the person The ideal candidate will be able to demonstrate the following: Completion of, or progress towards, relevant postgraduate qualifications and extensive relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and education. Significant experience in business analysis, process mapping, re-engineering, continuous improvement and organisational change, including analysing complex problems and developing practical solutions. Extensive knowledge of contemporary approaches to customer service (preferably in a higher education setting), with demonstrated experience using administrative systems and data analysis to improve service delivery to students. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to build strategic and trusted working relationships with a diverse range of technical and non-technical stakeholders. Proven project management skills, including the ability to set achievable, time-bound tasks from strategic and tactical objectives, and to work autonomously and in a team, managing multiple tasks under tight deadlines. Salary details The salary for this full-time position commences at $116,195.70 per annum plus 12% superannuation per annum. Additional information Position-related enquiries can be directed to Tanya Cook, [email protected] or 07-5595 1172. Application and submission details For further details regarding this appointment, please reference the Position Description and Selection Criteria. Click Apply Now and Create New Account to get started. You can: Upload your Resume – your account will be created automatically, or Manually enter your details to set up your account. Please ensure your application includes: A current resume A cover letter addressing the Selection Criteria outlined in the Position Description above For current Bond University staff, apply directly via People Connect , log in with staff credentials, from the Home dashboard select Careers, select the role and apply. If you require any assistance with your application submission, please visit Applying for jobs at Bond . Applications close: 11:59pm, Monday 16 November 2026 Applicants must have current work rights in Australia at the time of application. This status will be verified as part of the recruitment process. Pre-employment checks: Appointment is subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks (including working rights verification, reference checks and a certified copy of your highest qualification). In line with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence 2025, preferred candidates must complete a Gender-Based Violence (GBV) Declaration, and any offer of employment will be conditional upon the University’s review of the declaration. For more information, please visit our website via this link: Applying for Jobs at Bond Conditions of employment are offered under a Bond Workplace Agreement (BWA). Bond University is an equal opportunity employer, and we encourage our students and staff to respect individuality and diversity. In line with Bond University’s values, people from diverse backgrounds, women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, people who identify as LGBTIQ+, and people with a disability are encouraged to apply for positions at the University. Bond University Privacy Policy # Eligibility criteria or membership fees apply *Australian Financial Review’s Best Universities Ranking 2024 APPLY NOW Applications close: 16th November 2026 Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Read more about our acknowledgment of country Facebook LinkedIn Instagram TikTok YouTube Twitter WeChat Weibo Bond University Privacy Policy Disclaimer CRICOS Provider Code 00017B TEQSA Provider ID PRV12072"
