ulty of Society & Design Transformation CoLab Academic calendar Census dates Manage your enrolment Subject finder Timetables Enrol in your subjects Changing your subjects Changing your program Withdrawing or taking a break Compassionate or compelling circumstances Withdrawal without penalty Cross institutional study Unique Student Identifier (USI) Fees and other costs Payment methods Transcripts and documents Assessment and grades Exams Assessment timetable Deferred exams Grades Review of results Academic integrity Academic misconduct and how to avoid it Generative Artificial Intelligence (Gen-AI) guide for students and staff Casual Room Bookings Services and support Bond Connect Academic Skills Centre Student Affairs and Service Quality Bond Business School Bond University College Attendance requirements Faculty of Health Sciences & Medicine Faculty of Law ​Indigenous student support Indigenous Student Success Program Nyombil Indigenous Support Centre International student support Medical and health services Student counselling Accessibility and inclusion Accessibility resources Feedback and questions University security Escape | Hide | Tell Emergency contacts Career Development Centre About the Career Development Centre Careers information for all our current students Employers and Industry Global experiences Graduates and alumni Verification of qualifications What's On Preventing and responding to gender-based violence Wellbeing services Student Wellbeing Advisors JP/Commissioner for Declarations service LGBTIQ+ services and support Campus life Bond University Student Association Student clubs Faculty Student Associations Bond University Business Students' Association Health and Sport Sciences Student Association (HSA) Medical Students Society of Bond University (MSSBU) Law Student Association Society & Design Student Association Club events Student events Students living on campus Sports Centre Smoke-free campus Merchandise Store Student Services and Amenities Fee Bond Sports Centre Group exercise classes Personal training Sports Centre memberships Student housing options Student rights and responsibilities Complaints involving the behaviour of others Advocacy and support Appeals Your responsibilities Your rights Student conduct and misconduct Student surveys Graduate Outcomes Survey Student Experience Survey Opportunities Outbound student mobility Partnering with DFAT Exchange at Bond Participating institutions Asia Europe North America Information sessions Exchange blog How to apply Financial information and funding New Colombo Plan Scholarship 2027 Preparing to go Overseas Back at Bond Frequently asked questions Mooting at Bond What is mooting Mooting opportunities Mooting accolades Grants and scholarships Elite Athlete Fund Student Hardship Grant Student Opportunity Fund Frequently asked questions FinTech Hub training Bond Legal Clinics Program The Bond Law Clinic Climate Sustainability Clinic Criminal Law Clinic How to apply Internet Law Research Clinic My Community Legal Clinic Beyond Bond Graduation Preparing to graduate Conferral dates Ceremony information Ceremony videos Graduation booklets Graduation documents MyBond Library iLearn Staff iLearn Library Email Staff Intranet Online Service Catalogue Careers at Bond People Connect Alumni About Bond alumni Online Bond community The Arch Industry and partners Global education partners Sponsorship opportunities News and events News Events Contact Getting to Bond University Campus map Parking Close Home Job vacancy Jobs at Bond Applications Administrator Start of main\n      content. Applications Administrator Full-time, Continuing Appointment Reference number: 201413250 About the position As Australia's first private University, Bond University based at Robina, Gold Coast seeks to be recognised internationally as a leading independent university, imbued with a spirit to innovate, a commitment to influence and a dedication to inspire tomorrow's professionals who share a personalised and transformational student experience. Support student systems and data administration across the University. Administer and configure student systems to support users effectively. Monitor, troubleshoot and improve system performance and processes. Join Australia’s number one University for teaching*, and enjoy staff benefits including: Free staff car parking Salary packaging options for FBT and Non-FBT items# 17.5% of base salary leave loading Staff wellbeing program Free & Confidential Employee Assistance Program available for all staff Study assistance for staff and dependents# Corporate health and finance discounts Onsite Medical Centre and Counselling Services Onsite Sports Centre including gym, fitness classes and pool# The Applications Administrator will act as a key support resource in the Student Systems and Data team. The team is responsible for the administration and updates to the student management system used by Bond University, the timetabling system, the student placement system, the student wellbeing systems, the student portal and reporting to Government on student data. The Applications Administrator will be assigned to provide support in delivering dedicated software solutions to university stakeholders, enabling business improvement, data accuracy and effective system maintenance. This role requires collaboration across the university, including Student Business Services, Information Technology Services, the Student Success and Wellbeing team and the University’s faculties and academic units, to ensure optimal value is derived from core systems. The role is also responsible for system configuration, system health, and daily operational support including performance monitoring, data integration and reporting from the support systems. The primary focus of the role is supporting the InPlace Student Placement Management System, and the suite of Symplicity products (Advocate, Access, UniHub & CSM) used by the Registrar’s portfolio and other designated student facing and support roles and organisational areas. However, support to other applications may be required as business needs arise across the Student Systems and Data team. About the person The ideal candidate will be able to demonstrate the following: Completion of a bachelor’s level qualification in Information Technology and/or relevant work experience. Extensive experience within a professional ICT environment covering planning, administering, maintaining, and supporting business applications and data security. High-level problem-solving skills, including the ability to proactively develop innovative solutions. Sound understanding of technical IT issues to enable discussions with internal and external technical specialists. Experience in managing third-party vendor suppliers and issue resolution. Strong technical writing skills with proven ability to maintain comprehensive written system documentation. Ability to monitor continuous data integrations and perform relevant data cleansing for raised exceptions. Demonstrated experience in defining and optimising business processes. Strong cross-functional relationship management skills, including excellent written and oral communication skills. Salary details The salary for this full-time position commences at $99,108 per annum plus 12% superannuation per annum. Additional information Position-related enquiries can be directed to Tanya Cook, [email protected] or 07 55951172. Application and submission details For further details regarding this appointment, please reference the Position Description and Selection Criteria. Click Apply Now and Create New Account to get started. You can: Upload your Resume – your account will be created automatically, or Manually enter your details to set up your account. Please ensure your application includes: A current resume A cover letter addressing the Selection Criteria outlined in the Position Description above For current Bond University staff, apply directly via People Connect , log in with staff credentials, from the Home dashboard select Careers, select the role and apply. If you require any assistance with your application submission, please visit Applying for jobs at Bond . Applications close: 11:59pm, Monday 16 November 2026 Applicants must have current work rights in Australia at the time of application. This status will be verified as part of the recruitment process. Pre-employment checks: Appointment is subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks (including working rights verification, reference checks and a certified copy of your highest qualification). In line with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence 2025, preferred candidates must complete a Gender-Based Violence (GBV) Declaration, and any offer of employment will be conditional upon the University’s review of the declaration. For more information, please visit our website via this link: Applying for Jobs at Bond Conditions of employment are offered under a Bond Workplace Agreement (BWA). Bond University is an equal opportunity employer, and we encourage our students and staff to respect individuality and diversity. In line with Bond University’s values, people from diverse backgrounds, women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, people who identify as LGBTIQ+, and people with a disability are encouraged to apply for positions at the University. Bond University Privacy Policy # Eligibility criteria or membership fees apply *Australian Financial Review’s Best Universities Ranking 2024 APPLY NOW Applications close: 16th November 2026 Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Read more about our acknowledgment of country Facebook LinkedIn Instagram TikTok YouTube Twitter WeChat Weibo Bond University Privacy Policy Disclaimer CRICOS Provider Code 00017B TEQSA Provider ID PRV12072"
    },
