d Sports Centre Group exercise classes Personal training Sports Centre memberships Student housing options Student rights and responsibilities Complaints involving the behaviour of others Advocacy and support Appeals Your responsibilities Your rights Student conduct and misconduct Student surveys Graduate Outcomes Survey Student Experience Survey Opportunities Outbound student mobility Partnering with DFAT Exchange at Bond Participating institutions Asia Europe North America Information sessions Exchange blog How to apply Financial information and funding New Colombo Plan Scholarship 2027 Preparing to go Overseas Back at Bond Frequently asked questions Mooting at Bond What is mooting Mooting opportunities Mooting accolades Grants and scholarships Elite Athlete Fund Student Hardship Grant Student Opportunity Fund Frequently asked questions FinTech Hub training Bond Legal Clinics Program The Bond Law Clinic Climate Sustainability Clinic Criminal Law Clinic How to apply Internet Law Research Clinic My Community Legal Clinic Beyond Bond Graduation Preparing to graduate Conferral dates Ceremony information Ceremony videos Graduation booklets Graduation documents MyBond Library iLearn Staff iLearn Library Email Staff Intranet Online Service Catalogue Careers at Bond People Connect Alumni About Bond alumni Online Bond community The Arch Industry and partners Global education partners Sponsorship opportunities News and events News Events Contact Getting to Bond University Campus map Parking Close Home Job vacancy Jobs at Bond Events Administrator Start of main\n      content. Events Administrator Full-time, Fixed Term Appointment for 2 years Reference number: 201412043 About the position As Australia’s first private, not-for-profit university, Bond University based in Robina on the Gold Coast seeks to be recognised internationally as a leading independent university, imbued with a spirit to innovate, a commitment to influence and a dedication to inspire tomorrow's professionals who share a personalised and transformational student experience. Join a collaborative and dynamic Events team at a leading university Showcase your highly developed organisational and communication skills Enjoy great staff benefits, central location and free staff parking Join Australia’s top university for teaching* and enjoy staff benefits including: Free staff car parking 36.75 hour standard work week Access to flexible work/work from home arrangements# Up to 18/26 weeks of parental leave# Salary packaging options for FBT and Non-FBT items# 17.5% of base salary leave loading Staff wellbeing program Free & Confidential Employee Assistance Program available for all staff Study assistance for staff and dependents# Corporate health and finance discounts Onsite Medical Centre and Counselling Services Onsite Sports Centre including gym, fitness classes and pool# Reporting to the Events Manager, the Events Administrator will plan, deliver and evaluate a varied portfolio of recruitment and engagement events that support the University’s events marketing, recruitment and sales initiatives. Working with stakeholders across faculties and departments, as well as external vendors, sponsors and corporate partners, you will help ensure every event is delivered consistently and successfully. You will coordinate all aspects of event delivery on campus and offsite, from catering, audio visual, theming, registration and VIP management through to risk documentation and budget tracking. The role also provides financial and administrative support, including purchase orders, invoicing and post-event reporting, manages the sourcing and procurement of Bond merchandise, and serves as a key point of contact for event-related enquiries. This is a full-time role based on a 36.75-hour week. Because event schedules vary, some flexibility is needed, including occasional evening and weekend work during key events. About the person We are looking for a highly organised events professional who thrives in a fast-paced environment and enjoys bringing events to life. To be successful in this role, you will bring: A relevant undergraduate degree in event management, business administration, marketing, communications or a related discipline 3–5 years’ experience in event management, including event coordination, stakeholder engagement, sales support, hospitality operations, marketing and budget administration Strong administrative and organisational skills, with the initiative to manage multiple events concurrently and meet competing deadlines independently Excellent written communication skills, including drafting invitations, event publications, correspondence and budgets Proficiency in Microsoft Office, Zoom and event systems, with an eye for identifying sales opportunities and improving work systems A customer-focused, collaborative approach and the ability to work effectively with academic staff, students and colleagues Previous experience in a tertiary environment, and knowledge of event management, CRM and registration systems, will be highly regarded Salary details The salary for the position commences at $85,707.07 per annum, plus 12% superannuation. Please note: The fixed term of this employment contract will be for up to two years, with twelve months' probation. The prospect of conversion to a continuing employment contract will be discussed at the end of the contract term. Additional information Position-related enquiries can be directed to Hayley Martin, Events Manager on 0407755811 or [email protected] Application and submission details For further details regarding this appointment, please reference the Position Description and Selection Criteria Click Apply Now and Create New Account to get started. You can: Upload your Resume – your account will be created automatically, or Manually enter your details to set up your account. Please ensure your application includes: A current resume A cover letter addressing the Selection Criteria outlined in the Position Description above For current Bond University staff, apply directly via People Connect , log in with staff credentials, from the Home dashboard select Careers, select the role and apply. If you require any assistance with your application submission, please visit Applying for jobs at Bond . Applications close: 11:59pm, Tuesday, 17 November 2026 Applicants must have current work rights in Australia at the time of application. This status will be verified as part of the recruitment process. Pre-employment checks: Appointment is subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks (including working rights verification, reference checks and a certified copy of your highest qualification). In line with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence 2025, preferred candidates must complete a Gender-Based Violence (GBV) Declaration, and any offer of employment will be conditional upon the University’s review of the declaration. For more information, please visit our website via this link: Applying for Jobs at Bond Conditions of employment are offered under a Bond Workplace Agreement (BWA). Bond University is an equal opportunity employer, and we encourage our students and staff to respect individuality, inclusiveness and diversity. In line with Bond University’s values, people from diverse backgrounds, women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, people who identify as LGBTIQ+, and people with a disability are encouraged to apply for positions at the University . Please advise the Talent Acquisition Team if you require any reasonable accommodations to assist you at anytime during the recruitment process. For more information, visit Supporting diversity at Bond | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Bond University Privacy Policy # Eligibility criteria or membership fees apply *Australian Financial Review’s Best Universities Ranking 2024 APPLY NOW Applications close: 17th November 2026 Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Read more about our acknowledgment of country Facebook LinkedIn Instagram TikTok YouTube Twitter WeChat Weibo Bond University Privacy Policy Disclaimer CRICOS Provider Code 00017B TEQSA Provider ID PRV12072"
    },
