d Sports Centre Group exercise classes Personal training Sports Centre memberships Student housing options Student rights and responsibilities Complaints involving the behaviour of others Advocacy and support Appeals Your responsibilities Your rights Student conduct and misconduct Student surveys Graduate Outcomes Survey Student Experience Survey Opportunities Outbound student mobility Partnering with DFAT Exchange at Bond Participating institutions Asia Europe North America Information sessions Exchange blog How to apply Financial information and funding New Colombo Plan Scholarship 2027 Preparing to go Overseas Back at Bond Frequently asked questions Mooting at Bond What is mooting Mooting opportunities Mooting accolades Grants and scholarships Elite Athlete Fund Student Hardship Grant Student Opportunity Fund Frequently asked questions FinTech Hub training Bond Legal Clinics Program The Bond Law Clinic Climate Sustainability Clinic Criminal Law Clinic How to apply Internet Law Research Clinic My Community Legal Clinic Beyond Bond Graduation Preparing to graduate Conferral dates Ceremony information Ceremony videos Graduation booklets Graduation documents MyBond Library iLearn Staff iLearn Library Email Staff Intranet Online Service Catalogue Careers at Bond People Connect Alumni About Bond alumni Online Bond community The Arch Industry and partners Global education partners Sponsorship opportunities News and events News Events Contact Getting to Bond University Campus map Parking Close Home Job vacancy Jobs at Bond Research Coordinator Start of main\n      content. Research Coordinator Full-time, Fixed Term for 2 years Reference number: 201413636 About the position As Australia’s first private, not-for-profit university, Bond University based in Robina on the Gold Coast seeks to be recognised internationally as a leading independent university, imbued with a spirit to innovate, a commitment to influence and a dedication to inspire tomorrow's professionals who share a personalised and transformational student experience. Be part of an institution that fosters cutting-edge research and innovation Collaborate with leading scholars and researchers in your field of expertise Join a prestigious institution with a long-standing tradition of academic excellence Join Australia’s top university for teaching* and enjoy staff benefits including: Free staff car parking 36.75 hour standard work week Access to flexible work/work from home arrangements# Up to 18/26 weeks of parental leave# Salary packaging options for FBT and Non-FBT items# 17.5% of base salary leave loading Staff wellbeing program Free & Confidential Employee Assistance Program available for all staff Study assistance for staff and dependents# Corporate health and finance discounts Onsite Medical Centre and Counselling Services Onsite Sports Centre including gym, fitness classes and pool# The Research Coordinator leads and coordinates the University’s research funding support function, supporting the delivery of Bond University’s research strategy, strengthening external funding performance and researcher capability. The position liaises with Faculties, administrative staff and researchers, providing advice and support on funding identification, interpretation of complex scheme requirements, eligibility and compliance, proposal positioning and development, budget preparation, partner documentation, internal approvals and compliant submission. Key responsibilities: Research Funding Support: Identify and promote external funding opportunities and provide specialist advice to researchers on funding schemes, eligibility, strategic positioning and application development. Grant Application Coordination: Coordinate major national, international, industry and philanthropic funding applications, including proposal development, budget preparation, partner documentation, internal approvals and timely submission. Compliance and Quality Assurance: Interpret complex funding guidelines, undertake compliance checks, coordinate internal reviews and ensure applications meet sponsor requirements and University policies. Researcher Capability and Process Improvement: Build researcher capability through advice, workshops and resources, while improving pre-award processes, systems, tools and stakeholder engagement to enhance the quality and efficiency of research funding support. About the person The successful candidate will have: A relevant degree and substantial experience in research administration, research development or a comparable complex environment. High-level knowledge of national and international research funding schemes, including industry and philanthropic funding. Strong analytical skills and the ability to interpret complex funding guidelines, eligibility requirements, contractual provisions and governance requirements. Demonstrated experience coordinating complex funding applications, managing competing priorities and meeting strict deadlines. Proven ability to build relationships with academic staff and stakeholders, support researcher capability and develop high-quality, competitive grant applications. Excellent written and verbal communication, consultation and relationship-management skills. Salary details The salary for the position commences at $101,915.09 per annum, plus 12% superannuation. Please note: The fixed term of this employment contract will be for up to two years, with twelve months' probation. The prospect of conversion to a continuing employment contract will be discussed at the end of the contract term. Additional information Position-related enquiries can be directed to Lesley Hogan, Acting Director of Research Services, on [email protected] . Application and submission details For further details regarding this appointment, please reference the Position Description and Selection Criteria Click Apply Now and Create New Account to get started. You can: Upload your Resume – your account will be created automatically, or Manually enter your details to set up your account. Please ensure your application includes: A current resume A cover letter addressing the Selection Criteria outlined in the Position Description above For current Bond University staff, apply directly via People Connect , log in with staff credentials, from the Home dashboard select Careers, select the role and apply. If you require any assistance with your application submission, please visit Applying for jobs at Bond . Applications close: 11:59pm, Monday 23 rd November 2026. Applicants must have current work rights in Australia at the time of application. This status will be verified as part of the recruitment process. Pre-employment checks: Appointment is subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks (including working rights verification, reference checks and a certified copy of your highest qualification). In line with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence 2025, preferred candidates must complete a Gender-Based Violence (GBV) Declaration, and any offer of employment will be conditional upon the University’s review of the declaration. For more information, please visit our website via this link: Applying for Jobs at Bond Conditions of employment are offered under a Bond Workplace Agreement (BWA). Bond University is an equal opportunity employer, and we encourage our students and staff to respect individuality, inclusiveness and diversity. In line with Bond University’s values, people from diverse backgrounds, women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, people who identify as LGBTIQ+, and people with a disability are enco7uraged to apply for positions at the University . Please advise the Talent Acquisition Team if you require any reasonable accommodations to assist you at anytime during the recruitment process. For more information, visit Supporting diversity at Bond | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Bond University Privacy Policy # Eligibility criteria or membership fees apply *Australian Financial Review’s Best Universities Ranking 2024 APPLY NOW Applications close: 23rd November 2026 Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Read more about our acknowledgment of country Facebook LinkedIn Instagram TikTok YouTube Twitter WeChat Weibo Bond University Privacy Policy Disclaimer CRICOS Provider Code 00017B TEQSA Provider ID PRV12072"
    }
